==Trivia==
* The VIZ Media second edition of this volume was released on the same day as [[Chuang Yi]]'s translation of {{vol|Magical Pokémon Journey|10}} of [[Magical Pokémon Journey]].
*The cover of this volume is orange to celebrate the third anniversary of the release of Pokémon.<ref>Pokémon Adventures volume 5 Message from [[Mato]]: ''"This year ('99) is the third anniversary of the release of Pokémon on Nintendo [[Game Boy]]! And since the third-anniversary color is orange, there are limited edition orange Game Boys being sold. And that's why the cover for volume 5 is orange too!!"''</ref>

===Errors===
====VIZ Media second edition====
* {{p|Meowth}}'s name is misspelled as "Mewoth" on page 52 and {{p|Slowpoke}}'s name is misspelled as "Slowpoké" on page 63. On page 178, [[Silph Co.|Silph Company]] is misspelled as "Sylph Company".
* In the Elite Four recap on page 199, [[Agatha's Gengar]] is listed as [[Dewgong (Pokémon)|Dewgong]], likely due to [[Lorelei]]'s Dewgong being listed in the same format 4 pages earlier.
* At the end of the book on page 205, Raticate and Doduo are listed with levels from [[Pokémon Adventures volume 4|volume 4]] instead of their current ones.
** The same page also mistakenly lists Graveler's typing as {{2t|Normal|Ground}} instead of {{2t|Rock|Ground}}.

